  "title": "Sounds, greetings and courtesy",
  "note": "Polish is spelled almost exactly as it sounds, and stress falls on the next-to-last syllable. Watch these letters: ł = English w, w = v, ó = u, sz = sh, cz = ch, c = ts. ą and ę are nasal vowels. Say Pan (sir) or Pani (madam) to adults you don't know well.",
